#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:0209"
msgid "Run for cover. The Titans have gone mad! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:0296"
msgid "Run for your very life -- the ground shakes and the dead have come to the claim the city! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:031E"
msgid "Hold, you! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:0347"
msgid "Hold, stranger! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:036D"
msgid "Guardsman! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:03A1"
msgid "Aye. What do you want? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 043B:03C9"
msgid "Aye, stranger? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "What is the problem? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Bye. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is the problem? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0512"
msgid "That is what I wish to ask you! What do you know about Bentic the Scholar? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is the problem? "
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "What concern is it of yours? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "We have spoken. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "We have spoken. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "We have spoken. "
msgctxt "bark 043B:06AD"
msgid "Then know this: For conducting forbidden research, Bentic's head rests deep within the realm of the Lurker upon the command of the Lady Mordea. Know also that as his confidant all of your actions are under observation. Now answer this: What do you know of the fisherman named Devon? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Nothing. " or "I know nothing of Bentic. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Nothing. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Nothing. " or "I know nothing of Bentic. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "I know nothing of Bentic. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Nothing. " or "I know nothing of Bentic. "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0897"
msgid "You lie! You have been seen speaking to him. Know this: For conducting forbidden research, Bentic's head rests deep within the realm of the Lurker upon the command of the Lady Mordea. Know also that as his confidant all of your actions are under observation. Now answer this: What do you know of the fisherman named Devon? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Nothing. " or "I know nothing of Bentic. "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0997"
msgid "Then know this and be warned: For conducting forbidden research, the scholar's head rests deep within the realm of the Lurker upon the command of the Lady Mordea. Now answer this: What do you know of the fisherman named Devon? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I have met him. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "I have met him. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I have met him. "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0AE1"
msgid "Then let me also inform you that he has been placed under arrest and imprisoned. For your association with him you are also under suspicion. Be very careful whom you choose as friends from now on. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I have met him. "
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "May I go now? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why was Devon arrested? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Why was Devon arrested? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why was Devon arrested? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0BA6"
msgid "I do not have such answers. Ask him yourself! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Devon? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Who is Devon? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Devon? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0BF1"
msgid "Again you lie to me! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Devon? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0CFE"
msgid "Others have seen you with him, so do not pretend you have forgotten the fisherman. He has been placed under arrest and imprisoned. For your association with him you are also under suspicion. Be very careful whom you\tchoose as friends from now on. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What concern is it of yours? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0DC0"
msgid "Do not risk your worthless life with such boldness. Now answer the question! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What concern is it of yours? "
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "No! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No! "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0E82"
msgid "Then die for your insolence! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "What is your name? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0F56"
msgid "Never you mind such things. Better to be worried about your own hide. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is your name? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:0FE1"
msgid "What an odd question. 'Tis not -my- name that is important. You should be more concerned about your own business. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you guard? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "What do you guard? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you guard? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:106D"
msgid "What a peculiar mind for questions you have. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you guard? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:10AD"
msgid "I guard Devon and city, of course. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you guard? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:10EE"
msgid "I guard her Ladyship Mordea, of course! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where does this road lead? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Where does this road lead? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where does this road lead? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:11A3"
msgid "We have already discussed that, now haven't we. Do not waste my time. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where does this road lead? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:12A4"
msgid "You should know. I have seen you on your way to the cemetery. An eerie place, if you ask me, but your business is your own as long as you cause no trouble. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where does this road lead? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:12FA"
msgid "To the east lies the cemetery. An eerie place if you ask me. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where does this road lead? "
msgctxt "ask 043B"
msgid "Eerie? How eerie? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Eerie? How eerie? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:14EF"
msgid "'Tis not safe for sane men to be there. The cemetery is where the Necromancers inter the dead. Lithos may demand it, but I think it takes a twisted mind to perform the tasks they do. Some say that Lithos lets the Necromancers keep a few of the dead around to serve them. And late at night, I, myself, have often heard sounds that would freeze your bones. Beware to any who go there. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "May I go now? "
msgctxt "bark 043B:1588"
msgid "Yes, I have no more questions. Be off with you, and stay clear of trouble! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Bye. "
msgctxt "bark 043B:160F"
msgid "Aye. Enough of these questions. "
msgstr ""
